  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-10T18:35:00.771Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A feature to disable the dotted outlines around an object and the dotted line to it would be a very welcome quality of life change and an easy one to implement at that.\nWe already have vibration on collision of an object. We don't also need a visual representation around the object, especially when it renders over the top of avatars and breaks immersion. How many times have you accidentally been in the touch zone of a pillow when laying down and had an annoying blue line going to it.\nI'd like to see an option to remove this completely so we don't have to see these lines. Ultimately I think VRChat should be adopting more user customisable toggles for everything, in the event people who know exactly what they want can tailor the experience to themselves.",
